The hardware ID is reported by the DAC firmware at plug-in time; it is not assigned when you install a driver. Vendor ASIO drivers only accept VID/PID listed in their INF. This unit is currently bound to Microsoft's generic UAC2 driver, so ASIO Native cannot open. Use WASAPI (including DoP). If you need ASIO, ask the vendor whether this model has firmware that writes the official ID. Do not flash unofficial firmware.

