The hardware ID is reported by the DAC firmware at plug-in time; it is not assigned when you install a driver. Vendor ASIO drivers only accept VID/PID listed in their INF. This unit is currently bound to Microsoft's generic UAC2 driver. VID_20B1 is the usual XMOS reference-firmware vendor ID and is typically not in a brand's official device list. Use WASAPI (including DoP). If you need ASIO, ask the vendor whether this model has firmware that writes the official ID. Do not flash unofficial firmware.

